 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "footnote-4",
   "kind": "book",
   "number": "4",
   "html": "<p>see Dalibard and Cohen-Tannoudji, JOSA B, p2023 (1989) for further details.</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "c-early-1990s",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The first temperatures below the Doppler limit were measured in 1988, in sodium molasses (P. D. Lett <i>et al.</i>, Phys. Rev. Lett. 61, 169 (1988)), and Dalibard and Cohen-Tannoudji's explanation followed in 1989: the experiments belong to the late 1980s."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-td-hbar-gamma",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "By Eq. (8.96) the Doppler limit is $k_B\\kTD = \\hbar\\kgammaonetwo = \\hbar\\kgamma/2$ for a radiatively broadened atom; the book's $\\kTD = \\hbar\\kgamma$ leaves out Boltzmann's constant and the factor $1/2$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-large-detuning",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "Cooling needs red detuning, $\\kdelta < 0$, so the condition is $|\\kdelta| \\gg \\kgamma$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-omega-squared",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "$|\\kOmega|^2$ is meant: $\\kRopt = |\\kOmega|^2\\kgamma/((\\kgamma/2)^2 + \\kdelta^2)$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-capture-scaling",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "By Eq. (8.130) the Sisyphus capture velocity scales with the optical pumping rate $|\\kOmega|^2\\kgamma/\\kdelta^2$, not with the AC Stark shift $|\\kOmega|^2/\\kdelta$: at a fixed light shift it still falls as $1/|\\kdelta|$."
  }
 ],
